# ============================================================================
# Keystone — environment configuration
# ============================================================================
# Copy this to .env.local. You fill in:
#   1. SUPRSEND_SERVICE_TOKEN below, then
#   2. each workspace's 5 credentials from the dashboard (README step 4).
# Running `node --env-file=.env.local scripts/provision.mjs workspaces` creates the
# workspaces and writes labelled blank placeholders for those 5 credentials.
#
# .env.local is gitignored — your secrets never get committed.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED — your SuprSend ACCOUNT service token.
# (Dashboard → Account Settings → Service Tokens → generate → paste here)
SUPRSEND_SERVICE_TOKEN=

# The `workspaces` command APPENDS these per-workspace lines below. Paste each from
# SuprSend → the workspace → Developers → API Keys:
#   SUPRSEND_<WS>_WORKSPACE_KEY             "Workspace Key and Secret" → Workspace Key
#   SUPRSEND_<WS>_WORKSPACE_SECRET          same section → the Secret (shown once)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPRSEND_<WS>_PUBLIC_KEY    "Public Keys" → the SS.PUBK… value
#   SUPRSEND_<WS>_SIGNING_KEY_ID            "Signing Keys" → the signing_key_… UID (NOT ws_signk_…)
#   SUPRSEND_<WS>_SIGNING_KEY_B64           "Signing Keys" → Generate → the Base64 (shown once)

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — leave unset unless you need them:
#   SAFE_TEST_EMAIL_USER / SAFE_TEST_EMAIL_DOMAIN  where demo emails route
#                                                  (default: nikita+<name>@suprsend.com)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
